# Narrator: the Old Svalich Road and Tser Pool (docs/voice/narrator.md). Second person, present tense, one or two
# sentences. No rest lines here on purpose: rest triggers merge across regions and prefer conditioned variants, so a
# flag-conditioned rest line from this region would crowd out every other region's rests for the rest of the game.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The Ivlis crossroads

~ enter:svalich_crossroads
| The road crosses the river on a hump of old stone and comes to a crossroads with a signpost, a gallows and nobody else. The gallows, at least, has company.
| [night] The crossroads at night: a signpost, a gallows, and a field of low mounds that the dark has gone very quiet around.
| [flag.nicu_cut_down] The gallows rope hangs empty now, and the mound beside the road has settled. Crossroads are patient; this one will have another guest soon enough.
| [flag.crossroads_dead_cleared and not flag.nicu_cut_down] The field behind the gallows is a ruin of opened mounds. Nothing in it is getting up again, which is the most you can say for anywhere in this valley.
| [guest:ireena] Ireena slows at the crossroads and reads every arm of the signpost twice, as if it might have changed its mind about where things are.
cooldown 30

~ enter:crossroads_west_road
| The road runs west into darker trees, toward Tser Pool and, a long day beyond it, the walls of Vallaki.
once

~ enter:ivlis_bridge
| The bridge is older than the road on either side of it, and the river under it is the colour of strong tea. Something white turns over once in the current and is gone.
| [species:dwarf] {name} knows good masonry when it is under {name}'s boots: the bridge was built by people who expected it to be here for a thousand years. They were right, and gone.
once

~ enter:crossroads_gallows
| Low mounds in rough rows, no stones, no names: the people who were hanged here, put in the nearest ground. The grass grows thick on them. Grass does well on a gallows field.
| [flag.crossroads_dead_cleared] Every mound in the field has been opened from the inside. The grass lies flat around them, as if something very heavy got up and walked.
| [night and not flag.nicu_cut_down] The field is cold, colder than the night, and the mounds look less like mounds than like people lying very still with blankets pulled up.
cooldown 10

~ enter:crossroads_falls_track
| A rutted track climbs north beside the river. You can hear the falls long before you could ever hope to see them.
once

~ enter:crossroads_junction
| Four roads meet here, and none of them looks as if it wants you on it.
once

~ enter:crossroads_east_road
| East, the road runs back to the village. From here you can see the smoke of a few chimneys, and above them, on its cliff, the castle.
once

~ enter:crossroads_south_road
| The road south climbs between dead pines toward the castle. It is the best-kept road in the valley. Somebody wants it used.
once

~ examine:hanged_mens_field
| Mounds with no markers. The rope's work, buried where the rope left it. Somebody once tried to plant a little cross on one of them; it is lying in the grass.
| [class:cleric] Unblessed ground, and a great deal of it. {name} murmurs a word over the nearest mound, and the grass on it stirs, though there is no wind.

~ examine:crossroads_raven
| A raven sits on a fencepost by the road, very still, watching the crossroads the way a toll-keeper watches a bridge.
| [night] A raven on the fencepost, awake when ravens shouldn't be, with its back to the gallows field.

~ examine:ivlis_bridge_stones
| Names are scratched into the parapet, hundreds of them, by people waiting for someone to come along the road. Some of the newest have dates. None of the dates are recent.
| [class:wizard] {name} reads the scratched names out of habit. A few are in a hand {name} recognises: neat, crossing its sevens. AUREL WAS HERE. HE KNOWS.

~ examine:castle_road_view
| The castle stands on its spur of black rock against the sky, every window dark but one. The one is not a candle. You don't want to think about what it is.

~ examine:crossroads_milestone
| A milestone with the village's name chiselled off and a single word scratched in its place: TURN BACK. Under it, in a different hand: WHERE TO?

~ search:bridge_cache
| Wedged between two footing stones under the bridge, someone's emergency kit: a corked flask of red, wrapped in oilcloth, and nothing else. {name} pockets it, with a nod to whoever planned so well and didn't need it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Tser Pool

~ enter:tser_pool
| Fiddle music, woodsmoke, and laughter, real laughter, the first you have heard in this valley. Painted wagons ring a bonfire beside a dark pool, and a great patched tent glows from within.
| [night] The camp's fire is the brightest thing for miles, and the music carries far into the woods. Nothing in the woods seems to mind. That should tell you something about the camp.
| [flag.tser_pool_brawl_won] The camp is empty. The fire has burned to a red eye in the ashes, and the wagons stand with their doors open. Only the great tent still glows.
| [flag.nicu_kin_told and not flag.tser_pool_brawl_won] The fiddle is playing something slow tonight. When you come into the firelight, a few of the Vistani nod to you as if you were cousins.
| [guest:ireena] Heads turn as Ireena comes into the firelight, and the music falters for half a bar. Then the fiddler plays louder, as if to make up for it.
cooldown 30

~ enter:tser_road
| The Old Svalich Road runs past the camp under the pines. A track turns off it toward the firelight and the music.
once

~ enter:tser_pool_shore
| Tser Pool is black and perfectly still, though a stream pours into it from the north. The reflections in it are a beat behind the things they reflect.
once

~ enter:tser_horse_pen
| Horses in a rail pen, sleek and well fed, the best-cared-for living things you have seen in Barovia. They watch you the way the Vistani do: politely, and counting.
once

~ enter:tser_camp
| The camp smells of horses, plums and pipe smoke. Every wagon is painted in colours the valley has forgotten: red, gold, a green like summer.
once

~ examine:tser_bonfire
| A big, generous fire built by people who don't have to worry about firewood or who sees it. Its smoke goes straight up, which in this valley counts as a miracle.

~ examine:eva_tent_outside
| A tent of patched canvas the size of a cottage, painted with suns, moons and eyes. Candlelight moves inside it. The eyes painted nearest the flap have been retouched recently.

~ examine:vistani_wagons
| Little houses on wheels, carved and painted and hung with bells. Every door is shut. Every window has someone behind it.
| [class:rogue] {name} counts locks out of habit: good ones, and newer than the wagons. The Vistani trust the road. They don't trust the people on it.

~ examine:tser_pool_water
| The water is black and clear at once, the way a window is clear at night. The pool's bottom isn't visible. You are not sure there is one.

~ examine:vistani_horses
| Strong, glossy horses with plaited manes. One of them, a grey gelding, watches the road east and won't stop.

~ examine:wine_casks
| Casks of plum wine, chalked with dates. The oldest date is older than the walls of Vallaki. Somebody has been sampling it for quality ever since.

~ examine:ribbon_tree
| A pine hung with hundreds of ribbons, each knotted around a scrap of something: hair, a button, a dried flower. Every ribbon is a name, and every name is someone the road took.
| [flag.nicu_kin_told] A new ribbon hangs on the ribbon tree, knotted around a lock of black hair. It is the brightest red on the tree.

~ examine:tser_stream
| A cold stream comes down from the north, from Tser Falls, and slides into the pool without a ripple.

~ examine:tser_trough
| A trough of stream water for the horses, scrubbed clean. It is the only water in the camp that anyone drinks without thinking twice.

~ examine:tser_stewpot
| A black iron pot sits in the coals, and has sat there long enough to have a ring of soot like a tree has rings. It smells of plums and pepper.

~ examine:tser_grindstone
| A grinding wheel on a bench, worked by a foot treadle. A row of knives waits beside it, every one of them already sharp.

~ examine:tser_broken_cart
| A cart tipped on its side, one wheel cracked through and half rebuilt with new spokes. Fresh shavings lie in the mud around it.

~ examine:tser_charms
| A cord strung across the track, hung with bells, bones and little mirrors. Anyone who comes in from the road rings it, whether they want to or not.
| [class:cleric] {name} recognises a few of the charms: wards against the dead walking, and one that only asks the night to look elsewhere.

~ examine:tser_cairn
| A cairn of flat stones at the water's edge, each one scratched with a mark. The Vistani add a stone when the pool takes somebody. The cairn is taller than you are.

~ examine:tser_shrine
| A small wooden shrine at the water's edge, with candle stubs on its shelf and coins pressed into the wax. The candles face away from the pool.

~ search:tser_reed_dice
| Among the reeds, half sunk in the mud: a little leather bag of bone dice, and among them a yellow gem as big as a knucklebone, heavy as a fist of earth. Somebody staked it on a game here, and lost more than the game.

~ search:tser_pen_whistle
| Trodden into the mud of the pen, a horse-tender's whistle on a frayed cord. {name} rinses it off in the trough.

~ search:tser_stump_flask
| The old stump at the camp's edge is hollow. Inside, wrapped in a rag, is a corked flask that someone did not want Stanimir to know about. The cork is hot, and a thread of smoke leaks round it.

~ search:tser_wagon_cards
| Tucked up under the wagon's step on a nail: a deck of playing cards. Run a thumb along the edges and some of them are a little rougher than the rest.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Madam Eva's tent

~ enter:tser_pool_eva_tent
| Incense, candle smoke, and the dry smell of very old paper. Charms hang from every rope, turning slowly, though the air in the tent is still.
| [flag.eva_reading_done] The tent is as you left it. The five cards are back in the deck; the table remembers where they lay.
cooldown 20

~ enter:eva_tent_inner
| A low round table, a deck of cards, a chair, and an old woman who looks as if she has been sitting in it since before the tent was put up around her.
once

~ examine:tarokka_table
| The table is scarred with centuries of cards being laid down and taken up. The wood is worn into a shallow cross.

~ examine:eva_chest
| An iron-bound chest behind Madam Eva's chair, with a lock that is older than any key you have seen.
| [flag.tser_treasure_given] The iron-bound chest stands open and empty. Madam Eva has not bothered to close it; whatever it was waiting for has come and gone.

~ examine:tent_charms
| Bones, bells, little mirrors, a dried bird's foot, a child's tooth on a thread. Each one is turning, very slowly, to face you.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Tser Falls

~ enter:tser_falls
| The roar arrives before the view does. Then the trees open on a gorge, and the River Ivlis goes over the edge in one long white fall.
| [night] In the dark the falls are only a roar and a pale ribbon. Something on the far side of the gorge is howling, and the water is not quite loud enough to cover it.
cooldown 30

~ enter:falls_ledge
| The rock at the lip is slick with spray and very cold. Beyond it, nothing but white water and a long way down.
| [flag.falls_werewolf_slain] The lip of the falls is quiet now, apart from the falls. Long scratches in the rock show where the thing that waited here stood up.
cooldown 10

~ enter:falls_path
| The path is worn deep by many feet, all going one way and coming back again. People come to the falls to leave things.
once

~ enter:falls_west_glade
| A small glade with a cairn at its heart, out of the wind and the spray. It is the quietest place in the valley, which is not saying much.
once

~ enter:falls_east_glade
| Pines, ferns, and a pack lying in the bracken where somebody put it down and didn't come back for it.
once

~ examine:falls_tokens
| A boulder heaped with little offerings: buttons, a wooden doll, a rusted spoon, ribbons gone grey with spray. Barovians bring the falls something for the ones it took.
| [guest:ireena] Ireena looks at the doll on the offering stone for a long time, and doesn't touch it.

~ examine:falls_cairn
| A cairn of river stones, each scratched with a name. You count forty before you stop counting. The newest stone is blank; someone meant to come back and finish it.
| [name:kip_smudgewick] {name} reads every name on the cairn under his breath and leaves an apricot on the blank stone. It won't rot; he tries not to think about that.

~ examine:falls_marker
| A weathered marker stone with a carving of a woman in a long dress, falling. Someone has chipped away the face.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Road battlefields (random fights and events)

~ enter:road_ambush
| The road runs on between its ditches, open fields on both sides and stone walls tumbled into the grass. Plenty of room to see what's coming. Plenty of room for it to come.
| [night] The road at night: open fields, low walls, and a sky without a single star. Anything could cross those fields, and something is.
cooldown 0

~ enter:road_forest
| The road narrows between the pines, so close on both sides that the branches meet overhead. The forest is quiet, in the attentive way of a room where everybody has just stopped talking.
| [night] Under the pines at night the road is a pale stripe in the black. Your lantern makes a small room of light, and the forest leans in to look.
cooldown 0

~ examine:broken_cart
| A cart with a broken axle, half in the ditch, picked clean. The harness was cut, not broken. Whoever drove it left in a hurry, and on foot.

~ examine:fallen_trunk
| A pine as thick as a barrel lies along the edge of the road, felled long ago. Its upper side has been worn smooth by people sitting on it to rest, and by claws.

~ examine:claw_marked_pine
| Five long grooves in the bark, higher than a tall man can reach, and sap still beading in them. Fresh.
| [class:ranger] {name} lays a palm flat beside the marks. A wolf's claws, spread like a hand's. Whatever left them was standing up.

# --- Hidden finds (docs/story/found_magic_items.md) ---

~ search:cart_false_floor
| The broken cart's floor is a hand's width too high. Under the false boards, wrapped in sacking, lies a plain cloth bag that is much bigger on the inside than the out.
once

~ check:investigation:cart_false_floor:failure
| Splinters, a cracked axle and a smell of old turnips. Whoever drove this cart left nothing worth having. Or hid it well.

~ search:pine_satchel
| High in the claw-marked pine, a satchel hangs by its strap where something tore it from its owner. Inside, a pair of smoked-glass goggles that make the dark look like dusk.
once

~ check:perception:pine_satchel:failure
| Claw marks, sap and needles. Whatever climbed this tree, it didn't leave a note.

~ search:newer_mound
| One mound in the hanged men's field is newer than the rest, and shallow. Under a skin of earth, a pair of soft boots that make no sound when you set them down.
once

~ check:perception:newer_mound:failure
| Mounds and more mounds, all the same grey under the grass. Someone with sharper eyes might tell them apart.

~ search:humming_token
| Among the tokens left for the drowned, one is a pearl, and it hums against your palm like a held note.
once

~ check:perception:humming_token:failure
| Coins, ribbons, buttons and a child's tooth. Every token here was somebody's whole heart, and none of them is yours.

~ search:ribbon_tree_cache
| The roots of the ribbon tree have been dug under and packed back. In the hollow, wrapped in a Vistani shawl, a short bow of dark yew that strings sweeter than any bow should.
once

~ check:investigation:ribbon_tree_cache:failure
| Ribbons, roots and wishes. If the Vistani hide things here, they hide them where outsiders don't think to dig.

~ search:field_wall_cache
| Behind the field wall, under a flat stone, a farmer hid what he valued most: a pair of heavy iron gauntlets that make your arms feel like a bull's.
once

~ search:trunk_hollow
| The fallen trunk is hollow at one end. Inside lies a staff carved with scales, and when you lift it, it is warm and heavy as a living snake.
once

~ search:milestone_hollow
| Behind the milestone, a hollow packed with moss. In it lies a stubby wand of grey wood wound with something like spider silk.
once

~ search:cairn_necklace
| Among the names scratched on the cairn's stones hangs a necklace of glass beads, each one with a bubble of air trapped inside.
once

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Lane 28 (2026-10-08): the Tser Pool camp at work.

~ examine:tser_knife_stump
| An old stump chewed to splinters, with a knot dead in its middle that is chewed worst of all. Two knives are still in it.

~ examine:tser_deer
| A young deer hung by its back legs from a branch, half skinned, with the hide pegged out on the ground beside it to scrape.

~ search:tser_stage_bell
| In the mud behind the stage, a little brass bell on a broken ankle-string, the kind a dancer wears. {name} wipes it clean.
once

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Lane 28 (2026-10-08): the Svalich Woods.

~ examine:forest_log_2
| A pine brought down across the clearing by some old storm, its roots in the air like a hand. Moss has had years to climb it.

~ search:forest_cutter_stump
| A woodcutter's stump with a hand axe still bitten into it, the handle grey with weather but the blade as bright as the day it was forged. Whoever left it didn't come back to finish. {name} works the axe free.
once

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Lane 28 (2026-10-08): trees worth climbing.

~ examine:forest_climbing_pine
| An old pine scored by claws, with branches low and thick enough to climb. Ten feet up, you'd see over the brush to both bends of the road.

~ examine:ambush_lookout_tree
| A pine beside the road with planks lashed into it ten feet up, the rungs up the trunk worn smooth by hands and boots. Someone has sat up there before, watching for travellers.

# --- The open road's finds, once their first ones went into the story (Storyline QA, 2026-10-09) ---

~ search:cart_loose_board
| One board in the broken cart's bed lifts out. Under it, a twist of oiled paper holds a pinch of grey dust that drinks a puddle dry in a breath.
once

~ search:field_wall_gloves
| In a gap between the field wall's stones, someone tucked a pair of thin leather gloves. They grip the stone like a lizard's feet.
once

~ search:pine_ring
| Something winks from a high branch of the claw-marked pine: a plain bronze ring on a snapped thong, still warm. Its last owner jumped higher than the wolves, for a while.
once

~ search:trunk_wand
| Wedged in a split of the fallen trunk, a slim birch wand with a crystal set in its tip. Point it at anything enchanted and the crystal glows.
once

~ search:cutter_flask
| Behind the woodcutter's stump, a flask of something pale blue, still corked. It keeps the cold out of your hands just to hold it.
once

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Skill checks in the world (docs/story/world_checks.md)

~ check:animal_handling:horses_calm:success
| Under your hand the horses settle, but they keep shying from the reeds up the shore, where something flashes when the light finds it.

~ check:animal_handling:horses_calm:failure
| The bay snorts and turns its rump to you. Horses have long memories, and you are not in them.

~ check:performance:bonfire_dance:success
| The Vistani clap the time, the fire leaps, and for a little while nobody is thinking about the castle at all.

~ check:performance:bonfire_dance:failure
| You lose the beat, and the Vistani are kind enough to laugh with you, mostly.

~ check:sleight_of_hand:knife_game:success
| The knife flickers between your fingers faster than the Vistana can follow, and the coins are yours.

~ check:sleight_of_hand:knife_game:failure
| One stab too many, one finger too slow. The Vistani wince politely and keep the pot.

~ check:athletics:cart_lift:success
| You heave the cart up off its cracked wheel, and the floorboards shift: one of them was never nailed down.

~ check:athletics:cart_lift:failure
| The cart doesn't care how strong you are. It stays exactly where it is.

~ check:insight:ribbons_read:success
| Every ribbon is a name, except one knot, tied tight and low, which isn't a name at all but a promise to come back for what's buried beneath.

~ check:insight:ribbons_read:failure
| Names, and the people who tied them. Their grief is nobody's business but the tree's.

~ check:history:cairn_history:success
| The oldest marks at the bottom aren't names but a Vistani promise: the pool's people may pass the mists, and owe the castle for it.

~ check:history:cairn_history:failure
| Stones stacked with care, scratched with signs you can't read. They mean a great deal to somebody.

~ check:arcana:tokens_sense:success
| One token among the hundreds is warm to the touch and hums when you hold it near, like a held breath.

~ check:arcana:tokens_sense:failure
| Buttons, rings and bits of string. Each meant something to someone, and nothing to you.

~ check:athletics:pine_climb:success
| Up past the claw marks, where the branches thin, a satchel hangs from a broken limb, its strap snagged fast.

~ check:athletics:pine_climb:failure
| Two-thirds of the way up the bark peels away under your hand, and the ground comes to meet you.

~ check:religion:cairn_names:success
| You speak the names one by one, and under the last a stone rocks loose: someone hid a keepsake with their dead.

~ check:religion:cairn_names:failure
| The names are worn, and you stumble over them. The cairn keeps its own.

~ check:survival:mounds_earth:success
| Every mound has sunk the way old graves do, except one, piled higher and newer, as if someone dug it up and filled it in again.

~ check:survival:mounds_earth:failure
| Grass, weeds and mounds. The hanged keep their own counsel.

~ check:athletics:bridge_climb:success
| You find handholds in the old stone and climb down to the footings, where the river has wedged something in a gap above the waterline.

~ check:athletics:bridge_climb:failure
| A handhold crumbles, and the Ivlis takes you in up to the chest. It is very cold and very fast.

~ check:survival:castle_road_tracks:success
| Only one set of fresh tracks climbs the castle road: a heavy carriage, and horses that never paused to rest.

~ check:survival:castle_road_tracks:failure
| Mud, stones and old ruts. The castle road isn't telling you who uses it.

~ check:athletics:pine_lookout:success
| From the clawed pine's crown you can see across the clearing, where something glints high in the next tree.

~ check:athletics:pine_lookout:failure
| A branch you trusted gives way. The ground has been waiting.

~ check:survival:werewolf_marks:success
| These are a boundary, not an attack: renewed every full moon by something that walks upright. The trail runs north to the lake hills, and a hunter followed it.

~ check:survival:werewolf_marks:failure
| Deep claw marks, old and new. Something big, and you'd rather not know more.

~ check:athletics:hunters_platform:success
| The platform holds a dead hunter's stash of coin, and a warning cut into the rail for whoever climbs up next.

~ check:athletics:hunters_platform:failure
| The rungs are rotten two from the top. You get there eventually, by way of the ground.

~ check:athletics:wall_stones:success
| You lift the top stones off the tumbled wall, and in the gap beneath them someone has tucked a bundle out of the rain.

~ check:athletics:wall_stones:failure
| The wall has been falling down for fifty years and has no intention of hurrying for you.

~ check:medicine:bundles_cut:success
| You slit the old silk carefully, away from the venom-stained threads, and inside a dead traveller's purse is still tied to what's left of his belt.

~ check:medicine:bundles_cut:failure
| Your knife slips on the silk, and the venom on it finds the cut.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Road battle grounds (lane 3, 2026-10-12)
# Where the valley's and the woods' random fights may play out (story/road_grounds.gd).

~ enter:road_fork
| The road splits round a wooded knoll, and the signpost at the split leans as though it can't make up its mind either. On the knoll an empty gibbet cage turns on its chain.
| [night] Two roads run off into two darks, and on the knoll a cage creaks on its chain in a wind you can't feel.
cooldown 0

~ examine:fork_signpost
| Both arms have had their names scraped off, and somebody has cut a single word into the post instead: BACK. It doesn't say which way that is.

~ examine:fork_cairn
| A cairn of road stones on the knoll's crown, each carried up by a traveller who made it this far. Some of the stones have names scratched into them, and a few of the names have dates.

~ examine:fork_cage
| An iron gibbet cage on a dead branch, its door hanging open and its floor worn smooth. Whoever keeps it keeps it oiled.

~ examine:fork_cart
| A cart on its side, its sacks split and its horse long gone. The traces were cut, not snapped: someone left in a hurry and took the horse with them.

~ examine:fork_milestone
| A milestone worn too smooth to read, with a fresh notch cut into its top. Someone is counting something.

~ examine:fork_lookout
| A hunter's platform of lashed planks high in a pine, with rungs nailed up the trunk. From up there you'd see both roads, and anyone waiting on them.

~ enter:forest_clearing
| A clearing opens in the pines, all stumps, where the woodcutters took what they needed and stopped at a great oak nobody seems to have dared. Their fire is still warm.
| [night] The clearing at night: pale stumps like headstones, a fire burned down to red, and the oak's bough black against a starless sky.
cooldown 0

~ examine:clearing_oak
| An oak older than every pine around it, one great bough grown out level as a beam. The woodcutters felled everything else in the clearing; nobody has so much as carved an initial into this.

~ examine:clearing_fire
| A woodcutters' fire burned down to embers, a pot of something gone cold beside it. They left in the middle of supper, and they left their axes.

~ examine:clearing_log_1
| A log rolled up to the fire for a seat, worn smooth by a great many evenings. Tonight, by the look of it, nobody stayed long.

~ examine:clearing_axe
| A woodcutter's axe left sunk in a stump, its handle dark with use. Nobody leaves a good axe behind unless something made them.

~ examine:clearing_stand
| A hunter's platform up in a pine at the clearing's edge, the rungs on its trunk scuffed pale by boots. It looks down on the whole clearing, which is the point of it.

~ enter:road_ravine
| The road tips over the lip of a ravine, picks its way down a ledge of rock to a stream at the bottom and climbs the far wall the same way. Sheer stone on both sides, and whatever is down here with you has nowhere else to be.
| [night] The ravine at night is a black slot in the earth with a stream talking to itself at the bottom.
cooldown 0

~ examine:ravine_bridge_ruin
| The stumps of a bridge that once spanned the ravine, its timbers long since carried off by a spring flood. The road goes down and through now, the long way.

~ examine:ravine_rim_cairn
| A cairn at the head of the ledge path, built up a stone at a time by everyone who reached the bottom and came back up. It is not a tall cairn.

~ examine:ravine_lookout
| A hunter's platform lashed into a pine on the ravine's lip, looking straight down onto the ford. A good place to wait for deer, or for anything else that has to cross.

~ enter:stream_ford
| The road wades a quick brown stream at a gravel ford, the water knee-deep and loud over the stones. Upstream stand the footings of an old mill; downstream lies a cart that didn't make it across.
| [night] At night the ford is only sound: water over stone, and under it, now and then, something that isn't water.
cooldown 0

~ examine:ford_millstone
| A millstone cracked through the middle, lying in the grass where the mill used to stand. Someone built here and ground grain here, and then left nothing else at all.

~ examine:ford_cart
| A cart rolled over at the water's edge, one wheel still turning in the current. The stream took its load and is in no hurry to give it back.

~ examine:ford_rowboat
| A rowboat pulled up on the bank and chained to a stake, its oars missing. Whoever owns it means to come back for it.

~ examine:ford_lookout
| A hunter's platform high in a pine above the ford. From up there you'd see anyone crossing long before they saw you.

~ enter:wayside_shrine
| A roofless chapel stands beside the road, its walls fallen to stubs and its stone saints still keeping their corners. Someone has left fresh offerings at the altar, in a valley where nobody gives anything away.
| [night] The ruined chapel at night: candle stubs guttering on a cracked altar, and four stone saints watching the road instead of the sky.
cooldown 0

~ examine:shrine_pillar_1
| A stone saint at the chapel's corner, its face worn to a smooth oval by a century of weather. It still faces the road, as if expecting someone.

~ examine:shrine_saint
| A statue of a saint with its face struck off by a hammer, the chips still lying at its feet. The Morninglord's people built this chapel; somebody came by later to disagree.

~ examine:shrine_altar
| An altar split across by frost, with a sun cut into its face. The sun has been scratched through with a knife, carefully, over and over.

~ examine:shrine_offerings
| Bread, a twist of ribbon and a child's carved horse, left at the altar's foot within the last day or two. Somebody here still hopes, and you find you'd rather not know for what.

~ examine:shrine_gargoyle
| A gargoyle fallen from the chapel's roofline, lying on its back with its mouth open to the sky. It looks less like it fell than like it was thrown.

~ examine:shrine_post
| A little roadside shrine on a post, its painted saint peeling and its tiny roof furred with moss. A traveller's prayer hangs from it on a string, written very small.

~ enter:roadside_graves
| Behind a sagging fence the headstones climb the slope in crooked rows, leaning together like people sharing bad news. At the top a crypt waits with its door chained from the outside.
| [night] The graves at night: two lanterns at the gate, rows of stones going up into the dark, and somewhere among them the soft sound of earth being moved.
cooldown 0

~ examine:graves_crypt
| A family crypt with its name worn off the lintel and a chain across its door, padlocked from the outside. Outside is the side you'd want it locked from.

~ examine:graves_angel
| A stone saint weeping over the crypt, its tears worn into grooves by the rain. It has been crying here longer than anyone it mourns was alive.

~ examine:graves_open
| A fresh grave, dug and left open with the spade still standing in the spoil. It is waiting for someone, and in this valley it won't wait long.

~ examine:graves_spade_cart
| The gravedigger's handcart, loaded with shovels and a coil of rope. The gravedigger is nowhere to be seen, which in that line of work is a bad sign.

~ examine:graves_lantern
| A lantern on a post at the burial ground's gate, kept trimmed and kept full. Somebody walks up here every evening to see to it, and walks back down before dark.

~ scene:gallows_dead_turn
| Every head on the field turns the same way, toward the road, toward you. They do not hurry. They have all night, and the night is theirs.

~ scene:tser_tent_music
| Inside the great tent a fiddle starts up, the dancers turn in the lamplight, and for the length of one song nobody remembers what valley this is.
